course: dictionary
lesson: 8062
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the words around them show you which meaning is right. The word here is relation. «All our relations came for the party.» A party with everyone there fits family members, so relations means relatives.
explain: «The class studied the relation between speed and time.» Here relation means a connection: speed and time are linked, and one changes the other. In maths, a relation can also be a rule that links numbers, like «is greater than».
explain: «A preposition shows where or when one thing is in relation to another: under, on, after, before, between.» In relation to means about or compared with. Test it by swapping: «where or when one thing is about another» still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: «On the way he also went out of his way to spank a Hippopotamus who was no relation of his.» No relation means not family. Read the clue: the hippo is not part of his family, so the word means relative here too. Always check the clues before you choose a meaning.
fact: Relation can mean a family member, a connection between things, or a rule in maths.
fact: «Relations» can also mean how people get on: «good relations between neighbours» means neighbours who are friendly.
fact: «In relation to» means about or compared with.
fact: «A close relation» is a family member you are very near to, while «a distant relation» is one further away in the family.
fact: Quick check: swap your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
exercise: «All our relations came for the party.» What does relations mean here? | Friends from school | *Family members | A rule in maths | A connection between two things
exercise: «The class studied the relation between speed and time.» What does relation mean here? | Good manners | A pet | *A connection between two things | A family member
exercise: In maths, «is greater than» is a kind of what? | *Relation | Relative | Preposition | Holiday
test: «Friendly relations between the two countries helped them trade.» What does relations mean here? | *The ways the countries get on with each other | Rules for paying taxes | Family members from both countries | Maps of the world
test: «In relation to the other runners, Sam was the fastest.» What does in relation to mean? | Inside | *About or compared with | Far away from | Angry with
exam: «A hippo who was no relation of his» means what? | A hippo who was very hungry | *A hippo who was not part of his family | A hippo who ran away | A hippo who was his best friend
